# Master backend sync (mandatory)

Canonical shared backend for every frontend:

**https://github.com/ShamratX/master-backend-for-every-frontend**

## Rule

Whenever you **add, change, or remove** anything under Townloc `backend/` (Worker, CMS, API, migrations, `package.json` deploy scripts, related sync utilities that belong in the shared backend), you must also **update that master-backend repo** the same way — not only Townloc.

## Do

1. Port the same logic/files into `master-backend-for-every-frontend` (or the local clone if present).
2. Tell the user clearly what was synced vs Townloc-only (e.g. site copy in `cmsDefaults` that is Townloc-specific).
3. If you cannot access/push that repo in the session, stop and say so — do not leave master-backend stale silently.

## Townloc-only (usually no master sync)

- Static site HTML/CSS/JS under site root
- Townloc-specific marketing copy that is not shared Worker infrastructure
- One-off site scripts that only apply to `townloc.com` assets (confirm before skipping)

## Prefer asking once

If unsure whether a change is shared infrastructure vs Townloc-only copy, ask before skipping the master repo update.
